{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/862532-crazy-thoughts-about-pangaeans-and-changelings","id":862532,"title":"Crazy thoughts about Pangaeans... and Changelings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-09T02:39:06-07:00","id":862532,"title":"Crazy thoughts about Pangaeans... and Changelings","content":"Not sure whether to post this on Werewolf or Changeling, but this suddenly popped up into my mind - Pangaeans are the fundamental pillars of the world, as opposed to being aspects (Flesh) or reflections (Shadow) of it, right?<br /> <br /> The Gentry made deals with what I remember as being personifications of the aspects of the world to gain Contracts, right? But said aspects aren't Spirits, and they certainly don't seem to be walking around in Ironside...<br /> <br /> So, what if the entities the Strangers contracted with were Pangaeans??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5789-acanthus","name":"acanthus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T06:33:46-07:00","id":862573,"title":"","content":"Then one would kind of assume that the deals would end when the individual pangeans died, and where are these pangeans hiding, since Changelings can make new contracts to this day?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T08:29:23-07:00","id":862588,"title":"","content":"I think they were supposed to have made deals with aspects of the Wyrd, much like a Goblin Vow but more powerful. So they don't entreat Rose, the Beautius and Thorned, they entreat with the narrative function of roses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T08:47:15-07:00","id":862592,"title":"","content":"I had a musing last night that the True Fae might be the remnants of the Pangaean Story. It's possible Wyrd is a Pangaean in the shape of Arcadia, or Journey one in the form of the Hedge. Idigam might fit as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-09-2016, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T09:14:56-07:00","id":862607,"title":"","content":"At this rate, Pangaeans are going to be the next target for the &quot;X dominates the cosmology&quot; complaints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T09:19:52-07:00","id":862611,"title":"","content":"Ah it was just musings, what with the unending possibility. I'm sure anyone who would jump to that conclusion is already wrapped up in whatever they thought X was before Werewolf second edition came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T09:21:17-07:00","id":862612,"title":"","content":"Doubtful since they lack representation in the current setting. Any connection or importance beyond the Neolithic period is at best conjecture and folks looking for fan theories to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T09:23:30-07:00","id":862613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/862532-crazy-thoughts-about-pangaeans-and-changelings?p=862612#post862612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doubtful since they lack representation in the current setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, there is the Firstborn.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T09:34:51-07:00","id":862621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/862532-crazy-thoughts-about-pangaeans-and-changelings?p=862607#post862607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this rate, Pangaeans are going to be the next target for the &quot;X dominates the cosmology&quot; complaints.</div> </div> </div> </div>If people keep misapplying them the way they've been, yes, that would be a predictable outcome.<br /> <br /> They're decidedly not abstract and yet somehow people think the God-Machine \u2014 an entity that exists as the aggregate of a vast diversity of systems associated with those used by humanity, several of which are methods of organization rather than processes or classes of beings, or the guiding intelligence behind that aggregate \u2014 could be a modern Pangaean, despite the way the Machine acts like a parasite on established systems, has virtually nothing to do with the Shadow, is decentralized to the point of creating interference patterns within itself, and is incapable of communicating directly, all of which suggests that the absolute closest it gets to being remotely applicably called a Pangaean without taking something like your headcanon that loci are occult matrices as canon is in the same sense that the Hosts' driving imperatives are the Pangaeans the Spinner Hag and the Plague King are implied but never stated to have been.<br /> <br /> So I can see taking that notion and its neighbors seriously leading to a reaction against that overbroad application of terms, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T09:43:52-07:00","id":862626,"title":"","content":"Plus Satchel will be there to tell them how wrong they are.<br /> <br /> Still, a Machine is not abstract, and after Pangaea fell its natives were not only forced to become spirits. Just as the original God Machine Chronicle posited the God Machine as a machine-gone-amok, the Pangaean Machine could have, in the world of the flesh, continued being Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-09-2016, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T10:10:11-07:00","id":862637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/862532-crazy-thoughts-about-pangaeans-and-changelings?p=862621#post862621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If people keep misapplying them the way they've been, yes, that would be a predictable outcome.<br /> <br /> They're decidedly not abstract and yet somehow people think the God-Machine \u2014 an entity that exists as the aggregate of a vast diversity of systems associated with those used by humanity, several of which are methods of organization rather than processes or classes of beings, or the guiding intelligence behind that aggregate \u2014 could be a modern Pangaean, despite the way the Machine acts like a parasite on established systems, has virtually nothing to do with the Shadow, is decentralized to the point of creating interference patterns within itself, and is incapable of communicating directly, all of which suggests that the absolute closest it gets to being remotely applicably called a Pangaean without taking something like your headcanon that loci are occult matrices as canon is in the same sense that the Hosts' driving imperatives are the Pangaeans the Spinner Hag and the Plague King are implied but never stated to have been.<br /> <br /> So I can see taking that notion and its neighbors seriously leading to a reaction against that overbroad application of terms, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jiggers boys, it's the headcanon police!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:11:13-07:00","id":862720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/862532-crazy-thoughts-about-pangaeans-and-changelings?p=862592#post862592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a musing last night that the True Fae might be the remnants of the Pangaean Story. It's possible Wyrd is a Pangaean in the shape of Arcadia, or Journey one in the form of the Hedge. Idigam might fit as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, picture a Pangaean of the Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:53:57-07:00","id":862818,"title":"","content":"Definitely not a lake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}